"keykey.general.zhuyinLayoutHint" = "Where the 注音 symbols sit on the keyboard, effective immediately. Standard (大千) is the layout printed on Taiwanese keyboards and the one the original Yahoo! KeyKey shipped. Space is the first tone; 1–9 pick a candidate once the window is up. In 注音, associated phrases are always picked with Shift + a number — whatever the setting above says — because the number keys type 注音 there.";
"keykey.general.strokeConfirmation" = "Press Space to confirm the code";
"keykey.general.strokeConfirmationHint" = "In 速成, and in 倉頡 with the * wildcard, candidates appear before the code is finished, so Space flips to the next page instead of confirming what you typed. With this on, the first Space only confirms the code and keeps page 1 — press Space again to page, or 1–9 to pick. Plain 倉頡 is unaffected.";
"keykey.general.adaptiveCandidateOrder" = "Adapt candidate order based on your selections";
"keykey.general.adaptiveCandidateOrderHint" = "Applies to 倉頡, 速成, 注音 and associated phrases. Every candidate list is learned on its own: within a list, the candidates you have committed more often come first, and candidates you have committed equally often keep their built-in order. A 倉頡 code with a wildcard is learned separately from a complete code, and what is learned about 聯想字詞 is shared by 倉頡, 速成 and 注音. 拼音 keeps ranking candidates exactly as it did before. Turn it off for the built-in order — 五代 and 拼音 use their built-in rankings, 三代 and 注音 the original Yahoo! KeyKey order — which also pauses counting everywhere, without erasing what you have already learned.";
"keykey.general.language" = "Language";

