/* What's New pane (2.16.2) */
"app.whatsNew.summary" = "注音 now keeps up when you type without stopping. A number key that has no candidate on its row types 注音 again instead of disappearing, and a reading with only one character goes straight into your text without opening the candidate window — both the way the original Yahoo! KeyKey worked. Nothing changes in 倉頡, 速成 or 拼音.";
"app.whatsNew.changed1" = "In 注音, a reading with only one character is typed as soon as you finish its tone, without opening the candidate window, since there is nothing to choose. 聯想字詞 still follow it.";
"app.whatsNew.fixed1" = "In 注音, a number key no longer disappears when the candidate window has no candidate on its row. On the 標準（大千）keyboard 1 2 5 8 9 type ㄅ ㄉ ㄓ ㄚ ㄞ, so after a short list they now start your next character — 不, 的, 這 — and 3 4 6 7 correct the tone. A number with a candidate on its row still picks it.";

